g  other parts of the country have been  accelerated as quickly I think we're  seeing that earlier action before you've  got the loss of the of the virus you  can't contain it anymore  works so I'm hopeful that most the  country will be spared and we're  cracking down hard here in New York in  California as you mentioned earlier but  I'll tell you the most impressive bit of  news on this entire pandemic front  it was the paper from Marseille France  LA yesterday that many and I am sure my  colleagues are all stunned by they took  two old drugs a malaria drug and a  z-pack it's used for infections at  antibiotic and they demonstrated they  could reduce the viral load on people  within three days and all the virus was  gone in six days in  that's true and that's what the  president was speaking about yesterday  that dramatically changes everything  then all of a sudden we can suffocate  this virus much more rapidly it'll  behave more like the traditional  seasonal influenza and a lot of the pain  that we're anticipating going through  might not be needed dr. Manny are you  hopeful and optimistic as well dr. oz  puts an important element on the table  there absolutely I think that between  the programs that are being instituted  and just like dr. oz I'm very bullish on  this chloroquine protocol I think it has  shown at least in preliminary results  that it does decreases the viral load it  has a good scientific functionality when  it comes to viruses entering the cell  and is a drug that we have a lot of  experience with so I think that if we  continue and show promise that this is a  pathway to treatment or to prevention is  going to really change and make that  whole window a little bit shorter dr. oz  I want to throw up the White House  15-day guidelines because we are about  to hear from the White House again they  continue to alter and change their  guidelines or we've just seen them  evolve period over time but of course  the gatherings of more than 10 people we  are told to avoid those home-schooling  when possible avoid discretionary travel  avoid eating and drinking at bars  restaurants happening cuz so many have  shut down quarantine entire household if  one member is diagnosed focus on  protecting the vulnerable  obviously that message continues as well  but for so many dr. oz and I'm sure you  walk down the street or you get phone  calls from your page people can drive  themselves nuts with trying to keep  their house clean trying to prevent  their kids from seeing other kids when  they go out to play for a few minutes I  mean what is your message this morning  about how we can stay sane through all  this by while also protecting our family  you know over the last 24 hours  there I've seen a massive transition  from a period where doctors were yelling  and screaming with nurses and other  health experts say we got to pay  attention we got to get on this virus  and now I think we mostly are feeling  more optimistic than the average  American is I'm seeing more my late  friends and colleagues I'm hearing from  viewers who are more panicked than I  think is appropriate based on what I  know and I'm hoping many and other  doctors will be loud about this if we're  getting out  the mystic as doctors as clinicians you  should be feeling better about it as  well now we are seeing some potential  benefit by from in the Investor  community right they didn't sink the  stock market yesterday when we continue  to have worst number because everyone  has sort of expected this is the course  but I feel more bullish about this  process that I have in a long time in  part cuz this new data but also because  the government has finally done what we  knew would work and it will take time  you know when you're putting in when  someone we're gonna cause pain you can  do it fast you can do it slow you can  rip off the band-aid or do it slowly we  finally did we did it slowly but now the  band-aids on so let's manage they can  take the emotional issues we don't we  don't want to have the emotional  problems outweigh the true clinical risk  dr. mani do you share that optimism i I  do and you know for many for a couple of  days now I want it to be very optimistic  you know sometimes we become optimistic  and we get criticized by other by other  people because we say oh they're not  taking this serious we are taking this  serious we're you know we want the  social distancing we wanted the research  to go we want the federal government to  be prepared with any kind of potential  issues that they need to do and we want  the governors and the states to follow  through but we I am getting optimistic I  think that you know the shortages of  things that you know people are  predicting is gonna be you know it's not  going to be real in the short-term let's  say I think that these protocols  clinical protocols are going to make  some changes which are positive I look  at all the research that's being done by  biotech companies whether it's an you  know AB the plasma therapy where there  are these medications I think there's a  lot of good work coming out of this and  I think that we're gonna beat this  alright gentlemen we've got under a  minute so real quick lightning round to  both of you dr. Oz first about a week  ago when you talked about that balance  in terms of taking it seriously but not  panicking there were a lot of people  predicting look hospitals are about to  face this the dire consequences it's  gonna be so many new patients do you  think we're starting to turn the corner  we're starting to flatten that curve  that dr. Fox you talked about it's  impossible to tell and I don't know  about supplies my Hospital New York  Presbyterian is getting squeezed I'm  looking for masks and there's some  things we haven't thought about like the  blood banks are saying wait a minute you  know people still have to donate blood  for emergency cases some of the blood  products don't last that long so there  are things that we still need to manage  in the supply chain  but we will suffocate this pandemic  virus and it will not take us more than  the four weeks that most people expect  even if we have eight or ten weeks or  pain dr. mani last word  well I again I echo what dr. Oz says we  know we have to be vigilant we have to  keep the pressure on and we have to keep  the social distancing now we have to  focus on people that are staying home  children people with mental disabilities  that always concerns me a lot because  you know quarantine folks like that  sometimes it's a little problematic so I  think we have to multitask in this time  of need  stay inside those are doctor's orders we  got two of the best doctors right there  thank you for your advice this morning  we appreciate it thanks to both of you

